      {
        "id": "story",
        "type": "story",
        "provenance": "original",
        "title": {
          "en": "Steps of a staircase"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "Each step of a staircase is 15 cm higher than the one below. The heights 15, 30, 45, 60 ... follow a pattern: add the same amount each time."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "sequence",
          "AP",
          "common difference d",
          "a, a + d, a + 2d",
          "t_n = a + (n - 1)d",
          "t_10 = 32",
          "2b = a + c"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "A sequence is a list of numbers arranged in a definite order, such as 2, 4, 6, 8, ... Each number is a term.\nA sequence in which each term is obtained by adding a fixed number d to the previous term is an Arithmetic Progression (AP).\nThe fixed number d is the common difference: d = t2 - t1 = t3 - t2. It can be positive, negative or zero.\nIf the first term is a and the common difference d, the AP is a, a + d, a + 2d, ...\nThe general (n-th) term is t_n = a + (n - 1)d.\nFor the AP 5, 8, 11, ... we have a = 5, d = 3, so t_10 = 5 + 9 x 3 = 32.\nThree numbers a, b, c are in AP exactly when 2b = a + c, that is b is the average of its neighbours."
        }
      },
